<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>FitBuddy - Project Demonstration</title>
  <style>
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background: #f0fdfa;
      color: #134e4a;
    }
    header {
      background: #0f766e;
      color: white;
      text-align: center;
      padding: 28px 15px;
    }
    main {
      max-width: 750px;
      margin: 25px auto;
      padding: 0 15px;
    }
    section {
      background: white;
      padding: 20px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
      box-shadow: 0 3px 12px #0001;
    }
    li { margin: 10px 0; }
    .check {
      display: flex;
      gap: 10px;
      align-items: start;
    }
    .check input {
      margin-top: 6px;
      width: 18px;
      height: 18px;
    }
    button {
      background: #0f766e;
      color: white;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 12px 18px;
      cursor: pointer;
      margin-top: 15px;
    }
    progress { width: 100%; height: 18px; }
    #result { line-height: 1.7; }
    footer { text-align: center; padding: 20px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <h1>FitBuddy 💚</h1>
    <h2>Phase 7: Project Demonstration</h2>
    <p>Project Presentation and Demo Checklist</p>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section>
      <h2>Project Overview</h2>
      <p>FitBuddy is a student project that demonstrates a
      fitness planning interface with selectable goals and
      sample workout suggestions.</p>
      <p><b>Technologies:</b> HTML, CSS, JavaScript</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Seven Project Phases</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Ideation Phase</li>
        <li>Requirement Analysis</li>
        <li>Project Design</li>
        <li>Project Planning</li>
        <li>Project Development</li>
        <li>Project Documentation</li>
        <li>Project Demonstration</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Demonstration Checklist</h2>
      <p>Tick each item after checking it.</p>

      <label class="check">
        <input type="checkbox" class="demo-check">
        <span>Explain the project objective.</span>
      </label>
      <label class="check">
        <input type="checkbox" class="demo-check">
        <span>Show the website design.</span>
      </label>
      <label class="check">
        <input type="checkbox" class="demo-check">
        <span>Demonstrate the fitness goal selection.</span>
      </label>
      <label class="check">
        <input type="checkbox" class="demo-check">
        <span>Explain the technologies used.</span>
      </label>
      <label class="check">
        <input type="checkbox" class="demo-check">
        <span>Present testing and future improvements.</span>
      </label>

      <p id="progressText">Completed: 0 of 5</p>
      <progress id="progressBar" value="0" max="5"></progress>

      <button onclick="showSummary()">Show Demo Summary</button>
      <div id="result" aria-live="polite"></div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Conclusion</h2>
      <p>FitBuddy demonstrates how web technologies can be used
      to build a simple fitness planning interface. AI features
      require separate backend integration and testing.</p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>FitBuddy | Student Project</footer>

  <script>
    const checks = document.querySelectorAll(".demo-check");

    function updateProgress() {
      const completed = [...checks].filter(c => c.checked).length;
      document.getElementById("progressText").textContent =
        "Completed: " + completed + " of " + checks.length;
      document.getElementById("progressBar").value = completed;
    }

    checks.forEach(c => c.addEventListener("change", updateProgress));

    function showSummary() {
      const completed = [...checks].filter(c => c.checked).length;
      document.getElementById("result").textContent =
        "You completed " + completed + " out of " +
        checks.length + " demonstration checklist items.";
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
